        "block2": {
          "blockType": "markdown",
          "title": "About the Sleep Hygiene Study",
          "content": "The Study of Sleep Hygiene and Health is a citizen science research project investigating how smartphone use — particularly before bedtime — influences sleep quality, duration, and overall sleep hygiene.\n<br />By combining wearable device data, smartphone usage information, and short daily questionnaires, we aim to better understand the relationship between digital behaviour and sleep in real-world settings.\n<br />Partners: King's College London, South London and Maudsley NHS Foundation Trust.\n<br /><br />\n<button variant='contained' href='https://www.kcl.ac.uk/'>Learn more</button>"
        }
      }
    },

