      },
      "noCard": true,
      "content": {
        "block1": {
          "blockType": "hero",
          "title": "Our Aims",
          "content": "Smartphones are now an integral part of daily life. Many people use their phones before bed — for social media, messaging, gaming, or watching videos. However, it is not fully understood how different types of phone interactions influence sleep."
        },
        "block2": {
          "blockType": "markdown",
          "title": "Investigate whether increased screen time before sleep is associated with: Delayed sleep onset, Shorter sleep duration, Reduced sleep efficiency\n<br />Examine whether different app categories (e.g., social media, gaming, productivity) have different effects on sleep\n<br/>Compare sleep patterns across different age groups\n<br/>Explore long-term sleep behaviour over several months",
          "content": "Our goal is to generate evidence that can inform healthier digital habits and improve sleep hygiene recommendations."
        }
      }
    },

